A3d — corrected (array handling)
fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(tagStr, "CMDB_Portfolio:Claims")
| expand tags
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tags}
| sort hosts desc
| limit 300


If toString(tags) also complains, use this instead:

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags
| filter arrayIndexOf(tags, "CMDB_Portfolio:Claims") >= 0
| expand tags
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tags}
| sort hosts desc
| limit 300

A3e — all Claims hosts, all namespaces (the real scope)
fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "claim")
| expand tags
| filter startsWith(tags, "APMID:")
   or startsWith(tags, "[Azure]APMID:")
   or startsWith(tags, "[Environment]APPID:")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{tags}
| sort hosts desc
| limit 300


This is the one that produces your Claims APM ID list — every APMID tag found on any host that carries any Claims-related tag.

A3f — normalized APMID (collapse the namespace variants)
fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, entity.name, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "claim")
| expand tags
| filter contains(tags, "APP000") or contains(tags, "APP002")
| fieldsAdd apmid = if(contains(tags, "APMID:"),
                       splitString(tags, "APMID:")[1],
                       else: tags)
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{apmid}
| sort hosts desc
| limit 300


